# RSI Rule Alignment

Treat `CLAUDE.md` as the project source of truth for agent behavior.

## Required startup reads

1. Read `memory/MEMORY.md`, then read each memory file listed there.
2. Read `lab/sim/rules.py` before writing any simulation code.
3. Follow the run contract in `memory/run_definition.md`.

## Run contract

- One run = one TP (`tp_r`), one config, one window, one symbol set.
- TP sweep is not standard behavior.
- If TP changes, create a new run.

## Project boundaries

- Use only project-local paths under `RSI/` for memory, data, scripts, and output.
- Use `data/backtest.sqlite` as the default DB path.
- Keep active work in canonical folders (`lab/`, `scripts/`, `simulation/`, `cache/`, `memory/`).
- Treat `deprecated/` as archived-only unless explicitly asked to restore.

## Strategy constraints

- BAL+MED is rejected; do not include in new studies.
- Respect one-position-per-symbol and EXIT-time chunk assignment.
- Follow S1-S4 canonical stream definitions in `CLAUDE.md` and `memory/project_live_streams.md`.
